<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110216" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φᾰλός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>white,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Cf. Skt. <i>bhālam</i> 'brightness, forehead',
			Welsh <i>bal</i> 'having a white spot on the forehead', etc.)
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stammering, deaf, stupid,</i> Id. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαλίπτει</span> and perh. Old Slav.
				<i>z[ucaron]l[ucaron]</i> 'wicked', Skt.
			<i>hva/rate</i> 'to be crooked', etc.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
